 attention than a typical Indiana Republican hold.\n\nSpartz shows signs of vulnerability: a July poll sponsored by Democratic interests had her ahead by just two points, and she trails Ford in cash on hand despite raising more overall. National Democrats have targeted the seat, and Equality PAC has endorsed Ford. The forecast expects Spartz to win by a moderate margin, with meaningful uncertainty given thin and dated polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1386, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1359, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1346, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1263, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1331, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1305, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1313, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1321, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1281, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1641, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.1655, "margin": -6.0}]}